<title>UK: EU grants German intervention rye.</title>
<headline>EU grants German intervention rye.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The EU grains management committee on Thursday granted 42,379 tonnes of German intervention rye for export at a minimum selling price of 99.06 Ecus, member state officials said.</p>
<p>Bids for intervention barley from Sweden and Finland were rejected.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
